---
id: org.dxos.plugin.handpan
name: HandpanPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

Handpan music notation and real-time note detection for `DXOS` Composer. Phase 1 (this document)
is the audio-analysis layer and a `Tuner` that calibrates the detector to an instrument and shows
notes — and chords — as they are played. Notation (Song / Segment / Bar) is Phase 2; see
`docs/DESIGN.md` for the roadmap and the analysis techniques considered.

## Notes (Phase 2)

- `Song` / `Segment` / `Bar` ECHO schema with inherited key and time signature
- Notation grid editor and article surface; register with `composer-app`
- Record mode: strikes and tempo quantized into bars

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`        |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`        |
| `scenario`  | `org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0`    |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0`   |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`        |

## Types

```mdl
type Scale
  desc: A set of playable pitches; the ding is the handpan's central note.
  fields:
    id: string
    name: string               # e.g. "D Kurd"
    ding?: Pitch               # scientific pitch notation, e.g. "D3"
    notes: Pitch[]             # tone fields, any order (sorted ascending for notation)
```

```mdl
type NoteEvent
  desc: |
    A resolved strike: an onset followed by its pitch, measured from a long window after the onset
    minus an equal window before it, so notes still ringing do not bias it.
  fields:
    time: number               # onset, seconds since the analyzer started
    frequency?: number         # Hz; absent when percussive
    clarity: number            # 0..1
    velocity: number           # peak RMS after the onset
    partials: number[]         # harmonics 1..n, normalized
    peaks: SpectralPeak[]      # new energy, including fields ringing in sympathy
    percussive: boolean        # a tak/slap: no pitched note
    precise: boolean           # full note window available (cents are reliable)
    chord?: Pitch[]            # notes struck together; only in chord mode
```

```mdl
type NoteTemplate
  desc: A calibrated note — the reference Live mode and chord detection match against.
  fields:
    pitch: Pitch
    frequency: number          # median of the calibration strikes
    partials: number[]
    peaks?: SpectralPeak[]     # merged over strikes; attributes resonance to this note
```

## Components

```mdl
component Tuner
  desc: |
    Calibrates the detector to an instrument and displays notes as they are played. Pure
    component: owns its audio session; takes no app-framework capabilities.
  props:
    source: 'microphone' | 'synth'   # synth: pads strike synthesized tones (no instrument needed)
    defaultMode?: 'calibrate' | 'live'
    defaultScale?: string            # scale id; later changes switch the tuner
    strikes?: int                    # strikes recorded per note during calibration; default 3
    persist?: boolean                # keep scale, calibration, gain, sensitivity in local storage
    silent?: boolean                 # analyze synthesized strikes without playing them
    chords?: boolean                 # start with chord detection on
  state:
    mode: 'calibrate' | 'live'
    calibration: CalibrationState
    gain: number                     # dB, -12..+36
    sensitivity: number              # 0..1
  layout: |
    [mic] [scale ▾] [tak] [↺] [chords]            [Calibrate|Live]
                      3  C4
                 ─────●─────  (±50¢)
    [ oscilloscope ................. ] ▮ level
    Gain 0 dB ───●──      Sensitivity 70% ──●──
                  (handpan: ding + tone fields)
                  status · strike log · history
```

```mdl
component HandpanLayout
  desc: Top-down pan; ding centre, fields zig-zag ascending from the bottom.
  props:
    notes: ScaleNote[]
    target?: Pitch                   # calibration target (blue outline)
    active?: Pitch[]                 # sounding now (filled)
    progress?: Record<Pitch, number> # calibration progress ring; complete = success colour
  emits:
    onSelect(note: ScaleNote)
```

```mdl
component NoteDisplay
  desc: Current note (or chord, or Tak) with a ±50 cent meter; dimmed once nothing sounds.
```

```mdl
component LevelMeter
  desc: Input level on a dB scale with the "sounding" threshold marked.
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Note detection
  req F-1.1: Onsets are detected by spectral flux on a peak-normalized spectrum, independent of
    input level down to -30 dBFS strikes.
  req F-1.2: A strike's attack and tone bloom within 100 ms of each other are one strike.
  req F-1.3: Each strike's pitch is measured from 8192-sample windows either side of the onset; a
    note struck while others ring is measured within 5 cents.
  req F-1.4: Strikes without a clear pitch are reported as percussive (tak).
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Calibration
  req F-2.1: The user strikes each note of the scale in turn (ding first); the target advances
    after the configured number of accepted strikes.
  req F-2.2: Each strike is logged with its outcome: accepted (with cents), a different note, no
    clear pitch, or struck too soon after the previous note.
  req F-2.3: Octave and twelfth readings are folded back onto the target.
  req F-2.4: Calibrated notes are drawn in the success colour; calibration can be reset or a
    single note redone by selecting its pad.
  req F-2.5: With persist, the scale and calibration survive a reload.
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Live
  req F-3.1: The displayed note switches only after several consistent frames and is released
    after silence; the pad is lit only while the note sounds.
  req F-3.2: Gain and sensitivity are adjustable while listening, with tooltips.
  req F-3.3: Input level is shown against the sounding threshold.
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Chords
  req F-4.1: With chords on, a strike is decomposed against the note templates (NNLS); notes
    struck together are reported as one chord (e.g. "1+3") and all their pads light.
  req F-4.2: Learned templates attribute sympathetic resonance to the struck note.
  req F-4.3: Known limit — an octave pair (e.g. D3+D4) is reported as the lower note unless the
    upper note is about as loud.
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: Overlapping notes are measured precisely
  given: the nine D Kurd notes struck 0.3 s apart (each still ringing at the next strike)
  then: nine events, each precise and within 5 cents of its note
```

```mdl
scenario T-2: Calibration advances
  given: a calibration of two notes with two strikes each
  when: each note is struck twice in tune
  then: calibration is complete and has templates for both notes
```

```mdl
scenario T-3: Resonance is not a chord
  given: templates calibrated on a pan whose partner fields ring 3 dB below the struck note
  when: each note is struck alone with that resonance
  then: each chord contains only the struck note
```

## QA

Executable tests. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`). The plugin has no app surface yet
(Phase 2), so the flow runs in storybook; there are no operations to bind.

```mdl
test QA-1: Calibrate and play in the simulated session
  desc: |
    The primary journey with synthesized audio, so it needs no instrument: calibrate every note,
    then play notes, a tak and a chord in Live mode.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-2.1, F-2.4, F-3.1, F-4.1]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - storybook serves this worktree on port 9009
    - the story plugins/plugin-handpan/components/Tuner › Simulated Session is open with
      args silent:true (synthesized notes are analyzed without sound)
  steps:
    - name: Start
      do: Click the mic button.
      expect: the button turns red and the status reads "Play note D (D3)"
    - name: Calibrate every note
      do: Click each blue-outlined pad in turn until none is outlined.
      expect: every pad is drawn in the success colour and the status reads "Calibration complete"
    - name: Play notes
      do: Click Live, then pads 3, 1 and 5.
      expect: the display reads 3, 1, then 5; the matching pad lights while each note sounds
    - name: Play a tak
      do: Click Tak.
      expect: the display reads "Tak" and the history ends "T"
    - name: Play a chord
      do: Turn on Chords; strike pads 1 and 3 within 100 ms (a script dispatching two clicks).
      expect: the display reads "1+3" and pads 1 and 3 light together
  after:
    - name: Stop
      do: Click the mic button.
      expect: the button is no longer red
```
